<title>PHILIPPINES: PHILIPPINE SEC FINES FOUR BROKERAGE FIRMS.</title>
<headline>PHILIPPINE SEC FINES FOUR BROKERAGE FIRMS.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) had penalised four brokerage firms after they were found to have mishandled the investments of a client, SEC chairman Perfecto Yasay said.</p>
<p>&quot;(The SEC) has already come up with the decision penalising the brokers concerned, finding them to have violated our rules,&quot; Yasay told a news conference on Thursday.</p>
<p>Fines ranging from 50,000 to 350,000 pesos each were imposed on the firms.</p>
<p>Yasay said the four brokerage houses - Abacus Securities Corp, Dharmala Securities, Lippo Securities and Sapphire Securities - had 15 days to appeal the decision.</p>
